  "R161_cost": 5455.09331771126,
  "R161_decision": {
    "status": "STOP_CURRENT_RN_REPLACEMENT_RESEARCH_ONLY_DEFAULT_OFF",
    "conclusion": "The complete physical RN objective is integer/objective preserving, but neither RN-core nor the sole uniform RN-P revision is competitive with the declared OLD whole-native control on these two sources. Keep the research entry default off and stop this finite study without entering the conditional complete E+/N-RN panel.",
    "reason": "All six finite MIPs execute meaningful integer search under the same 4096-node capacity and 900s outer allowance, each ending TIME_LIMIT. OLD dominates both RN versions in final verified physical U and qualified L on RX35 and NB35. RN-P raises both continuous LP bounds, but its integer outcomes remain inferior: RX35 U/L=.406923269363301/.173456239045039 versus OLD .401139788438118/.210751964941072; NB35 U/L=.497425087324243/.378710952495425 versus OLD .463426190476191/.388764524132733. Auxiliary column counts are equal and the smaller matrix does not provide a compensating useful cost/search tradeoff. Lower Native Work on NB35 is reported, not treated as a win when both endpoints are worse. The decision uses full finite integer-search evidence, not root weakness alone.",
    "next_question": "Stop investing in this RN-core/RN-P expression on the present evidence. A future structural study would first need a useful quantitative bound on reciprocal covariance/distortion implied jointly by the original stock, e-penalty and physical scope. The fixed-denominator limit and elementary distortion bound identify a falsifiable condition; merely having a new factor t does not justify a split controller. The present penalty-only tightening excludes saved LP points and raises roots but does not yield competitive whole-native outcomes. No automatic S/t buckets, old+RN cut intersection, route-flow replacement, larger R160 blocks, passive archive or late-feedback project is started.",
    "major_revisions_used": 1,
    "further_recipe_revision": false,
    "complete_panel_entered": false,
    "complete_method_candidate_frozen": false,
    "complete_method_H_calls": 0,
    "complete_method_helper_calls": 0,
    "fresh_Eplus_runs": 0,
    "historical_main_comparison_CSV_changed": false,
    "stable_GI_TBC_B_default_unchanged": true,
    "scope": "Two existing own-H/R83 sources, one Gurobi Seed, matched complete-root Native development. RN-P reuses this round's paid unchanged OLD controls with verified model/Start and Native object equality; it is not a new same-PE panel.",
    "not_claimed": [
      "universal RN impossibility",
      "stable promotion",
      "independent confirmation",
      "P-GRB superiority",
      "complete Eplus versus N-RN performance"
    ]
  },
